For the first season, the review aggregation website [[Rotten Tomatoes]] reported a 76% approval rating, with an average rating of 6.8/10 based on 54 reviews. The website's consensus states, "''The Gifted''{{'}}s first season lays a solid foundation for an involving superhero drama that powers past the origin-story doldrums by focusing on grounded, topical stories over mindless action and special effects."<ref name="TGS1RT" /> [[Metacritic]], which uses a weighted average, assigned a score of 63 out of 100 based on 22 reviews, indicating "generally favorable reviews".<ref name="TGS1MC" />

For the second season, Rotten Tomatoes reported an 83% approval rating, with an average rating of 6.8/10 based on 12 reviews.<ref name="TGS2RT" />

===Nazi allusions<span id="Comparison to Nazism"></span>===
Discussing the series, Drew Koch of ''[[Bustle (magazine)|Bustle]]'' magazine noted that it explored themes such as the persecution of minority groups, sacrificing freedom for safety, and criticizing "big government". He highlighted the antagonistic agency Sentinel Services, guessing the initials "SS" were a reference to the [[Schutzstaffel]], a paramilitary division of Nazi Germany.<ref name="AnalysisBustle">{{cite web|url=https://www.bustle.com/p/where-are-the-x-men-on-the-gifted-theyre-missing-for-one-big-scary-reason-2748298|title=Where Are the X-Men on the Gifted?|last=Koch|first=Drew|work=[[Bustle.com|Bustle]]|date=October 2, 2017 |access-date=November 19, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171201032847/https://www.bustle.com/p/where-are-the-x-men-on-the-gifted-theyre-missing-for-one-big-scary-reason-2748298|archive-date=December 1, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> [[USA Today]]'s Brian Truitt also noted this reference, and the character Polaris directly calling out the government agents as Nazis, along with the mutant underground being patterned after the [[Underground Railroad]].<ref name="AnalysisUSA">{{cite web|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2017/10/01/foxs-the-gifted-puts-modern-spin-x-men-metaphor/717655001/|title=Fox's 'The Gifted' puts a modern spin on X-Men metaphor|last=Truitt|first=Brian|work=[[USA Today]]|date=October 1, 2017|access-date=November 19, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171006154439/https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2017/10/01/foxs-the-gifted-puts-modern-spin-x-men-metaphor/717655001/|archive-date=October 6, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref>

